{# ============================================================================
   ROTATION — the authoring surface, ported from the design's
   configure.html#rotation.

   A CYCLE PER POST, OR PER TEAM: the ring of days a watch repeats for ever,
   and the month it generates. Exceptions are edited on the plan sheet and
   never here — "a pattern generates, a day is edited" is the whole authoring
   model, and this page is the first half of it.

   WHAT IS HERE TODAY: the register of every rotation the area declares, what
   each one's ring is, what it asks for per day, how big its pool is, how far
   it has generated and which posts run none at all. That is the half of the
   design that can be drawn from what is stored.

   WHAT IS NOT: the cycle EDITOR — the ring of day buttons, the preset select,
   the pool picker, the live generated month. It is a write surface with its
   own Stimulus behaviour, and it lands with the plan sheet it shares its
   vocabulary with. The register below is not a placeholder for it: it is the
   design's own third card, whole.
   ========================================================================== #}
{% extends '@UhifadhiRoster/configure/_frame.html.twig' %}

{% block roster_section %}

{% if chosen %}
    {# ============================================================
       THE CYCLE EDITOR — FULL ROW, ruled 2026-09-20. A cycle, a pool of
       five and a month cannot be configured in half a column, so the
       editor spans the row and the month it generates sits BELOW it.

       NOTHING IS WRITTEN UNTIL SAVE. Every control below mutates a draft
       held in the page and the form's one submit sends the whole thing —
       which is why the server validates it as one object and refuses a
       malformed ring whole, with a sentence.
       ============================================================ #}
    <form method="post" data-controller="roster--rotation"
          data-roster--rotation-draft-value="{{ draft|json_encode }}"
          data-roster--rotation-shifts-value="{{ shifts|map(s => {key: s.key, label: s.label})|json_encode }}"
          data-roster--rotation-candidates-value="{{ candidates|json_encode }}"
          action="{{ path(constant('Uhifadhi\\Roster\\Controller\\RosterConfigureController::SAVE_ROTATION_ROUTE'), {uuid: area.uuid, rotation: chosen.uuid}) }}">
        <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrfToken }}">
        <input type="hidden" name="draft" data-roster--rotation-target="draft">

        <div class="c rband">
            <div class="rb-hd">
                <span class="tab">The rotation</span>
                <span class="rb-ttl">
                    <b>{{ chosen.station ? chosen.station.name : chosen.teamName }}</b>
                    {%- if chosen.station and chosen.station.code %} <span class="mono">{{ chosen.station.code }}</span>{% endif %}
                    &middot; <span data-roster--rotation-target="summary"></span>
                </span>
            </div>
            <div class="rb-body">

                <div class="r-rotrow top">
                    <span class="fldlab">The cycle</span>
                    <div style="min-width:0">
                        <div class="r-cyc" data-roster--rotation-target="ring">
                            {# Server-rendered so the ring reads without JS. #}
                            {% for day in chosen.cycle.positions %}
                                <button type="button" class="{{ day == 'off' ? 'o' : 'd' }}" disabled><b>{{ loop.index }}</b><em>{{ day }}</em></button>
                            {% endfor %}
                        </div>
                        <div class="rfrag" style="border:0;padding:4px 0 0;margin:0">
                            <b>repeats for ever</b><em>day 1 is <time datetime="{{ chosen.anchoredOn.format('Y-m-d') }}" data-localtime-format="day">{{ chosen.anchoredOn.format('D j M')|lower }}</time> &middot; each person enters the ring one day later than the last</em>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="r-rotrow">
                    <span class="fldlab">Per day</span>
                    <span class="r-pool" data-roster--rotation-target="counts"></span>
                </div>

                <div class="r-rotrow top">
                    <span class="fldlab">Pool</span>
                    <div class="r-pool" data-roster--rotation-target="pool"></div>
                </div>

                <div class="r-rotrow">
                    <span class="fldlab">Day one</span>
                    <input class="fld" type="date" style="max-width:170px" value="{{ chosen.anchoredOn.format('Y-m-d') }}"
                           data-action="change->roster--rotation#field" data-roster--rotation-name-param="anchoredOn"
                           aria-label="The date day one of the ring falls on">
                    <span class="more">moving it re-plans the future</span>
                </div>

                <div class="r-rotrow">
                    <span class="fldlab">Stood down</span>
                    <span class="r-pool">
                        {% for weekday, label in {1: 'mon', 2: 'tue', 3: 'wed', 4: 'thu', 5: 'fri', 6: 'sat', 7: 'sun'} %}
                            <button type="button" class="r-pill{{ weekday in chosen.standDownWeekdays ? ' on' : '' }}"
                                    data-action="roster--rotation#toggleWeekday" data-roster--rotation-weekday-param="{{ weekday }}">{{ label }}</button>
                        {% endfor %}
                        <span class="more">a whole weekday the post stands down &mdash; not a hole</span>
                    </span>
                </div>

                <div class="r-rotrow">
                    <span class="fldlab">Rest rule</span>
                    <select class="fld" style="max-width:250px" aria-label="Rest rule"
                            data-action="change->roster--rotation#field" data-roster--rotation-name-param="restRule">
                        {% for rule in restRules %}
                            <option value="{{ rule.value }}" {{ rule == chosen.restRule ? 'selected' : '' }}>{{ rule.label }}</option>
                        {% endfor %}
                    </select>
                    <span class="more">a ring that breaks the rule generates a hole, never an illegal watch</span>
                </div>

                <div class="r-rotrow">
                    <span class="fldlab">Generate to</span>
                    <select class="fld" style="max-width:190px" aria-label="Horizon"
                            data-action="change->roster--rotation#field" data-roster--rotation-name-param="horizonDays">
                        {% for label, days in horizons %}
                            <option value="{{ days }}" {{ days == chosen.horizonDays ? 'selected' : '' }}>{{ label }}</option>
                        {% endfor %}
                    </select>
                    <span class="more">an edited day is never overwritten by a later run</span>
                </div>

                <div class="rfrag"><b>Nothing here is presence</b><em>a rotation says who is DUE &middot; who was actually there is the handset&rsquo;s check-in, and this page never writes one</em></div>

                {% if mayManage %}
                    <div class="staddrow"><span class="sp"></span><button type="submit" class="cta">Save the rotation</button></div>
                {% endif %}
            </div>
        </div>
    </form>

    <div style="height:12px"></div>

    {# THE MONTH IT GENERATES — the house calendar, below the editor and
       full width. A PREVIEW WRITES NOTHING: it is the same pure planner
       the generator runs, producing values rather than rows, so it cannot
       disagree with the result. #}
    <div class="c">
        <span class="tab">What it generates<span class="src">&middot; a preview &mdash; nothing is written</span></span>
        {{ atlas_calendar(previewFeed, previewMonth, previewScope) }}

        <div class="r-hz">
            {%- if chosen.generatedThrough %}
                <b>Generated to <time datetime="{{ chosen.generatedThrough.format('Y-m-d') }}" data-localtime-format="day">{{ chosen.generatedThrough.format('D j M')|lower }}</time></b>
            {%- else %}
                <b>Never generated</b><span>the ring has produced no duty yet</span>
            {%- endif %}
            <span class="sp"></span>
            {% if mayManage %}
                <form method="post" action="{{ path(constant('Uhifadhi\\Roster\\Controller\\RosterConfigureController::GENERATE_ROTATION_ROUTE'), {uuid: area.uuid, rotation: chosen.uuid}) }}">
                    <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrfToken }}">
                    <button type="submit" class="btn sm">Generate from tomorrow</button>
                </form>
            {% endif %}
        </div>
        <div class="rfrag"><b>Today is left alone</b><em>people are already standing today&rsquo;s watches, and regenerating the day underneath them would move somebody who is at a post</em></div>
    </div>

    <div style="height:12px"></div>
{% endif %}

<div class="c rband">
    <div class="rb-hd">
        <span class="tab">Every rotation in this area</span>
        <span class="rb-ttl"><b>{{ rotations|length }}</b> declared &middot; the area&rsquo;s other {{ postsWithoutARotation|length }} post{{ postsWithoutARotation|length == 1 ? '' : 's' }} run none</span>
    </div>
    <div class="rb-body">
        <table class="tbl">
            <tr><th>applies to</th><th>the ring</th><th>per day</th><th>pool</th><th>generated to</th></tr>
            {% for rotation in rotations %}
                <tr>
                    <td>
                        {%- if rotation.station %}
                            <b>{{ rotation.station.name }}</b> <span class="mono">{{ rotation.station.code ?: '—' }}</span>
                        {%- else %}
                            <b>{{ rotation.teamName }}</b> <span class="mono">per team{% if rotation.baseStation %} &middot; based at {{ rotation.baseStation.name }}{% endif %}</span>
                        {%- endif %}
                        {%- if not rotation.active %} <span class="fog">stood down</span>{% endif %}
                    </td>
                    <td>{{ rotation.cycle.positions|join(' · ') }}</td>
                    <td>
                        {%- for key, count in rotation.slotsPerShift -%}
                            {{ loop.first ? '' : ', ' }}{{ key }} {{ count }}
                        {%- else -%}
                            <span class="fog">&mdash;</span>
                        {%- endfor -%}
                    </td>
                    <td>{{ rotation.pool|length }}</td>
                    <td>
                        {%- if rotation.generatedThrough -%}
                            <time datetime="{{ rotation.generatedThrough.format('Y-m-d') }}" data-localtime-format="day">{{ rotation.generatedThrough.format('j M')|lower }}</time>
                        {%- else -%}
                            <span class="fog">never run</span>
                        {%- endif -%}
                    </td>
                </tr>
            {% else %}
                <tr><td colspan="5" class="fog">No rotation is declared in this area, so nothing is generated and no post is short.</td></tr>
            {% endfor %}
            {% for station in postsWithoutARotation %}
                <tr><td class="fog">{{ station.name }} <span class="mono">{{ station.code ?: '—' }}</span></td><td class="fog" colspan="4">no rotation &mdash; and therefore never a hole</td></tr>
            {% endfor %}
        </table>
        <div class="rfrag"><b>A post with no rotation is never counted, reported on or called a hole</b><em>the roster works the posts somebody put on its books, and says which ones those are</em></div>
        <div class="rfrag"><b>Nothing here is presence</b><em>a rotation says who is DUE &middot; who was actually there is the handset&rsquo;s check-in, and this page never writes one</em></div>
        <div class="rfrag"><b>An edited day is never overwritten by a later run</b><em>the generator steps over a day somebody has touched, whole &mdash; it does not merge or fill the gaps</em></div>
    </div>
</div>
{% endblock %}
